  "scope_limits": [
    "Exact 0.3.5 to 0.3.6 local service and desktop upgrade on an offline pristine Arch/Omarchy Linux/AMD64 owner-user stack. Earlier releases use documented intermediate upgrades. Remote installation, other distro runtime stacks and power cuts were not qualified here.",
    "Real QML update buttons use an exact-program guest-only polkit fixture, not human password entry. Setup receipts are reconstructed from genuine previous installer and SSH enrollment evidence.",
    "Guest bundle activation uses harness acknowledgements; separate private native QML tests cover actual hot/cold activation, failed-candidate recovery, preferences and restart. Stock updater interaction remains manual.",
    "Large logical preview checks use sparse fixtures, through the real client/server up to 8 TiB and exact published/candidate binaries above 100 GB in the guest. Only a small stopped fake is fully imported after removing the generated sparse fixture. No full 100 GB copy or throughput claim.",
    "No production pier, protected ship, ~/temp-ur, installed service/plugin or human DEV review state was used or changed. Storage accounting includes a 4 GiB reserve for 18 unreadable DEV directories, separately from the 4 GiB guest scratch allowance.",
    "Schema 47, desktop format 1, bootstrap API 1, runtime image and pill are unchanged. Identity, stopped-state, authorization, path, entry-count and full-content verification remain. Cross-host handoff stays capped at 100 GB."
  ],
  "policy": "Immutable frozen source and assets; protected source/race/QML/release-policy checks and merge commit required. No protection bypass or workstation upgrade."
